## World Coordinate System — Z-up Conversion (COMPLETE — engine, data, docs, and the signed-fabric recompose are all done and committed)

The Z-up effort is complete and committed; the former living working doc (`E:\Dev\COORD.md`) has been deleted now that all its work items are done. The durable record lives in git history, this section, the code, and the per-module `src/**/*.md` docs. This section is the resume-point summary (decisions D1-D4, per-seam detail).

**The decision.** Sneeze's world frame is now **right-handed, Z-up**: X=right(east), Y=forward(north), Z=up; ground = XY plane, height = +Z, gravity (later) = -Z. Rationale is renderer-agnostic (Sneeze models a physical world — the CAD/GIS/robotics/Blender category, which converged on RH Z-up / ENU). **Sneeze's contract is with ANARI, never with Filament** — ANARI imposes no world up (the `up`/`direction` are per-camera params), so Z-up is purely a Sneeze-side convention. The Y->Z change is benign for the current renderer because it is a rotation within the same handedness, not a mirror (winding/normals/culling intact).

**Decisions (all settled):**
- **D1 — Identity orientation: forward = +X (east), up = +Z**, shared by camera and lights. Models impose no forward (axis-align at import, D2); camera identity is browser-internal; **lights are the sole public identity contract** (an unrotated spot/directional shines toward +X, top toward +Z). +X chosen over +Y for math coherence (angle 0 = +X; textbook `atan2`). NOTE: +Y is still the *world-axis* label "north/forward" (ENU) — a different notion from a directional object's identity forward (+X).
